---
import { site } from "../../config/site";

const proofLines = [
  {
    value: site.proof.dealsWorked,
    text: "deals worked as a licensed broker",
    placeholder: true,
  },
  {
    value: site.proof.buyerConversationsPerWeek,
    text: "buyer conversations a week",
    placeholder: true,
  },
  {
    value: "",
    text: "Paid the same whether you close or walk away",
    placeholder: false,
  },
];
---

<section id="help" class="py-16 md:py-24">
  <div class="fade-in-section mx-auto max-w-[1100px] px-4 sm:px-6">
    <h2
      class="max-w-3xl font-serif text-3xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight sm:text-4xl"
    >
      I'm not a coach, a course, or a deal finder. I'm a broker who works deals
      every day.
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-prose text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      Most people selling help to business buyers have never sat on the other
      side of the table. I do it every day. I know what a broker is thinking
      when your email comes in, what makes a seller take an offer seriously,
      what a lender will actually approve, and what tends to kill a deal in
      week six. That's the perspective you're paying for.
    </p>

    <div
      class="mt-10 flex flex-col gap-4 border-y border-line py-8 md:flex-row md:gap-12"
    >
      {
        proofLines.map((line) => (
          <p class="text-base font-medium text-ink">
            {line.placeholder && (
              <span class="placeholder-value">{line.value}</span>
            )}{" "}
            {line.text}
          </p>
        ))
      }
    </div>

    <h3 class="mt-12 font-serif text-xl font-semibold">What I don't do</h3>
    <ul class="mt-5 flex max-w-prose flex-col gap-4 text-ink-soft">
      <li>
        I don't find deals for you. There are thousands of businesses listed
        publicly right now. Finding them is not the hard part. I help you tell
        the good ones from the rest, get to the front of the broker's line,
        and work the process.
      </li>
      <li>
        I don't run your due diligence. I help you build the team that does,
        and I tell you what to ask them.
      </li>
      <li>
        I don't take a commission or a percentage of your deal. Ever.
      </li>
      <li>
        I don't give legal, tax, or investment advice. I tell you when you need
        someone who does.
      </li>
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
